# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Only third-party leaks belong here. Anything IM itself allocates must be
# freed, and the sanitizer job exists to prove that -- so keep these matches
# as narrow as possible.
#
# x265 leaks ~1.2 KB per encoder from x265_encoder_open, reached through
# libheif's x265 plugin during heif_context_encode_image. IM releases the
# heif_encoder and the heif_context it owns; this allocation is below that
# and there is no API to reclaim it.
#
# Deliberately matched on x265 rather than libheif: a suppression for libheif
# would also hide IM failing to release a heif_image or heif_image_handle,
# which is exactly the kind of bug this job is here to catch.
leak:libx265
leak:x265_encoder_open
